Build test-devices-cdplaytrack or test-devices-cdplaytrack-quick. The native Amiga CD
device test group selects this regression. Run devices/cdplaytrack/cdplaytracktest
with an audio track numbered 2 present. The test checks ordinary and
upper-word-contaminated track/count fields, asynchronous playback, CD_INFO,
and rejection of counts whose low word is zero.

A disposable fixture can be generated from the repository root:

    python3 developer/debug/test/devices/cd/readahead/make_disc.py /tmp/cd-word-data.iso
    python3 - <<'PYTHON'
    from pathlib import Path
    Path('/tmp/cd-word-audio.bin').write_bytes(bytes(2352 * 75 * 20))
    Path('/tmp/cd-word.cue').write_text(
        'FILE "cd-word-data.iso" BINARY\n'
        '  TRACK 01 MODE1/2048\n    INDEX 01 00:00:00\n'
        'FILE "cd-word-audio.bin" BINARY\n'
        '  TRACK 02 AUDIO\n    INDEX 01 00:00:00\n')
    PYTHON

Mount /tmp/cd-word.cue in a stock CD32. Its silent audio track is sufficient:
the assertions inspect public playback state, not subjective sound output.
No game image is required. Exit 0 means all checks passed; failures return 20.
